# toolchain_skip_surface.baseline - ratchet for issue #3733:
# the runAotChecked toolchain-SKIP surface, frozen at the counts
# BELOW (they are EXACT, not a ceiling).
#
# The header used to name the counts in PROSE -- "2,046 call sites in
# 634 files at 2026-09-17" -- and that number was WRONG from the
# moment it was written: the writer emitted a FIXED string, so every
# --update re-stamped the same stale sentence over fresh counts
# (measured 2026-11-03: the baseline said 4,008 while the header
# still said 2,046). The counts are the machine-readable lines
# below; the header now only says where they are.
#
# Last re-baselined: 2026-11-03.
#
# Regenerate with scripts/check_toolchain_skip_surface.py --update
# after a burn-down step. --update REFUSES to raise absorbing_sites
# (it may only fall) and REFUSES to raise checked_calls while
# absorbing_sites RISES (a rise means a new absorbing call site,
# which is the defect the ratchet exists to catch). A FLAT
# absorbing_sites SANCTIONS a checked_calls rise — that is the rule
# the module docstring states ("only when absorbing_sites did not
# rise"), and the condition implements it.
#
# EXACT, not a ceiling: a count below its baseline fails as STALE
# HEADROOM (same rule as every sibling ratchet in this family).
#
# absorbing_sites : the violation count. Sites where a runAotChecked
#                   result reaches a "return on SKIP" guard with no
#                   positive rejection-text check (#3733).
# checked_calls   : the denominator. runAotChecked{,,Lenient,
#                   Disposal} calls in tests/**/*.cpp outside
#                   tests/support/. May rise legitimately when a
#                   new checked test is added (the test_main.cpp
#                   additive-field / run_parallel.sh floor wires
#                   the loud half).
# support_calls   : the control — same tokens, no filters. Differs
#                   from checked_calls only when a file moves into
#                   or out of tests/support/.
absorbing_sites = 0
checked_calls   = 4090
support_calls   = 4107
